Subject: [PATCH 19/31] Sync CameraXFrameSource exposure assist (F8)

CameraXFrameSource from Mosip26 1ec4f49 (Part 1: exposure assist for dim
faces). The engine jars and the model bundle are unchanged (same SHA-256
in engine-sync.txt).
- While delivering, the mean luma of the face region (centre 40% x 50% of
  the upright frame) is read from the copied Y plane. Below 70 for 1 s the
  camera's exposure compensation steps up (at most every 500 ms, up to its
  maximum); above 150 it steps back toward 0; stop() resets it to 0.
- On by default; setExposureAssist(boolean), exposureAssist(),
  exposureIndex(), lastCentreLuma(). The debug timing line shows the luma
  and the index.
- ExposureAssistTest (JVM, fake camera control): brief darkness changes
  nothing, the step rate and maximum, stepping back never below 0, reset,
  unsupported and fixed cameras untouched, disabling resets, and the
  face-region luma with rotation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
